alogue ever to be  uttered in the series but you can see  why Hamill wouldn't want to try and  deliver those words Hamill remembered  pleading for the lines removal out of a  sense of self-preservation this is  really not fair because you know we're  the ones that are gonna get vegetables  thrown at us not you the presence of the  planet names aqua ley and Sullust in the  convoluted line serves to demonstrate  just how much got chiseled away from  Star Wars script on its way from page to  screen in the original story treatment  aqua lay was a fleshed-out planet with  the real world parallel of communist  North Vietnam by the time the movie was  shooting the names had been reduced to a  reference for the sake of world building  when Hamill prevailed in removing the  one line they appeared in he deleted the  planets entirely the line that haunted  Hamill isn't the only part of Star Wars  original script that needed work and  Hamels not the only actor who had issues  Harrison Ford who plays the space pirate  in the film at one point threatened to  tie George up and and make him say his  own lines at gunpoint while the cast  complaints with the script may have  caused some friction their efforts  worked to sand down Star Wars rough  edges making it so most of the worst  stuff never made it out of the editing  Bay it all goes to show that when it  comes to collaboration compromise is  king  otherwise you get the Phantom Menace and  how many great lines can you quote from  that film Arthur no place is terrible  thanks for watching click the looper  icon to subscribe to our YouTube channel  plus check out all this cool stuff we  know you'll love to  [Music]
 

